Reason: torch 2.6 changed torch.load's default to weights_only=True, which refuses the PyG Data objects in TRIX's processed dataset caches (datasets.py) and the config dicts in its checkpoints (run_*.py, pretrain_*.py). Every torch.load in the pinned tree gets weights_only=False explicitly: the value that WAS the default on the pinned torch 2.1, so the cu118 image is unchanged in behaviour and the cu128 image (containers/incite/Dockerfile.cu128) can load the caches at all. Added 2026-09-02 for the second machine.

